<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5625" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bracchĭālis</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">brāch-</span></b> ), e,
			adj.
		bracchium, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the
			arm</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nervus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 5, 4, 99</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crassitudo,</span>”
				<i>the thickness of an arm</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 17, 27, § 123</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">torques,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vop. Aur. 7</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bracchĭāle</span></b> , is,
				n. (sc. ornamentum): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">argenteum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 28, 7, 23, § 82 sq.</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">25, 10, 80,
				§ 129</span></i>; <i><span class="en">32, 1, 3, § 8</span></i>; and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bracchĭālis</span></b> ,
			is, m. (sc. torques), Treb.
					<i><span class="en">Claud. 14, 5</span></i> (class.
			armillae); <i>an armlet</i>, <i>bracelet;</i> cf. <i><span class="en">Prisc. p. 1220</span></i>
		P.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
